A||||16||theogre||Business card?
Z||000000||theogre||08-29-99||09:44 PM||||After talking to someone I happened to see...... I came up with the following idea:<p>Why don't we create a biz card size thing that any member can print and leave on every Fiero we see?<p>It should be done very carefully. We DON'T want to come off as spammers. Maybe something like:<p>&gt;begin card<br>You own one of the most unusual cars on the planet. Do you own a computer? Here's where you can find a whole bunch of people that share your interest:<p>http://www.pennock.nl/forum.htm<p>This is a free service provided by a fellow Fiero owner.<br>&gt;end card.
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||08-30-99||12:54 AM||||Sounds like a great idea!<p>Too bad there are only 2 or 3 Fieros in my town. <IMG SRC="/ubb/frown.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>If anyone else is interested in doing this, I'd be more than happy to come up with a simple design for the cards.. Maybe a bunch of people could offer suggestions and we could vote? or each person who wanted to could design and use their own?<p>I've had some experience designing business cards before, though I get my cards printed professionally and the designs similar to the ones I've done before might not be suitable for printing at home. <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>I see other people posting really helpful ideas and information on here, and I really don't have much to offer as I still have a lot to learn about Fieros. I think it'd be really cool to design a card like this that all forum users can print and give out, so even tho it wouldn't be much, I'd still be doing something sort of useful. <IMG SRC="/ubb/wink.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>Here is one of my most recent cards, I have several more in my portfolio.<p> <IMG SRC="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/portfolios/images/lfbb-card.jpg"> 
Z||000002||Gokart||08-30-99||03:18 AM||||I think its a great idea! Everytime a see another Fiero I wonder if its just another car to him/her or do they appreciate it as much as I do mine, and are they armed with all the Fiero knowledge thats out there to keep their car looking and running tip top. Like the info and fun this forum provides. If its ok with Cliff, lets do it!! 
Z||000003||batboy||08-30-99||06:24 AM||||I stopped at a parts store a while back and one of the two cars parked in front was a nice red Fiero SE. I quickly figured out which guy in the store was the owner and chatted with him. Like most Fiero owners, he was proud of his car. Anyway, during this discussion we learned that both of us had stripped off parts from the dead Fieros in the local boneyard. Pretty cool.<p>I think that anyway to help unite Fiero owners together is good. Let's keep those few remaining Fiero in great running condition. I think some of these non-wrecked cars going to the salvage yard really ought to get restored instead. The more people that have access to a knowledge and parts base for Fieros, the more people will be encouraged to restore a Fiero instead of sending it to the grave.
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||08-30-99||08:21 PM||||Ogre,  I think that is a great idea. I sometime see Fieros that look lost and I want to take them home. I wonder if the owner has the info they need to keep them up. This idea will help all of our so loved little cars.<p>Iam with you on this one, lets do it.
Z||000005||lowCG||08-30-99||09:23 PM||||That's a great idea,like you said,you don't want to offend anyone that might really appreciate what we have here,so careful,non-salespitch wording would be needed.
Z||000006||kel||08-30-99||11:42 PM||||I like this idea!  Everytime I see another Fiero, which isn't too often, I wonder too if they appreciate this little gem as much as I do.  I'm definitely for it!
Z||000007||ChadMan||08-31-99||07:42 AM||||Our club (Central Ohio Fiero Enthusiasts) has printed up business cards like these that we leave on the windshields of Fieros we see.  We've gotten a lot of new members that way!
Z||000008||Ozzy||09-01-99||10:27 PM||||I think this is an excellent idea ogre. I can't give enough cudo's to this site and the kind of REAL help it has given me. <p>Being a mechanically inclined Fiero ignoramous, who also refuses to utilize the services of the best legalized extorsion racket going AKA the Automotive Repair Trade, I have learned many things here from you and the others who post here that equate to $$$$$$$$ saved. I don't know anyone who's not interested in that!<p>How to do it; Are not the simplest ideas usually the best? Keep the card simple in format and as non intrusive as possible. I would be willing to contribute some dollars toward this and also distribute the cards. Hell I generally will go out of my way just to talk to another Fiero owner if I have the time. There are about 12 Fiero's around this town that I've seen. (120,000 people)<p>Let me know if I can help with anything or when you have something, where I can get a hold of them. (would also be willing to pay for them if need be)<p> email:==&gt;  ozzy123@teleport.com<p><br>Ozzy
