Z||000014||DaRkLoRD||09-02-99||09:41 AM||||Another thought.. why not print the cards on normal paper, and then get them laminated? I live in a small town, and here I can get stuff laminated for a very reasonable price. <br>(it'd probably be similar or cheaper in cities.. and that is CDN amounts btw, USD are lower)<br>$1.00-$1.50 per sheet, and business card programs usually print 10 or 12 cards to a sheet, right?<br>The cards would not only stand up well in the rain, they'd look pretty cool too. The problem I see with getting cards printed professionally, is one person ends up with a bunch of them, and they'd most likely have to mail most of the cards to other forum members to distribute. 
